# tools/flip-ledger.jsonl — the anti-rot flip ledger (SDD §3.2, FR-4a-d).
#
# Append-only, git-tracked, NEVER truncated. This file is the durable evidence trail for every
# advisory-sensor promotion: an advisory immune sensor earns blocking (required-check) authority
# ONLY after it proves itself here, and can never rot back into a numb always-green gate because
# every promotion is grounded in an operator-adjudicated true-catch recorded below.
#
# WRITE MODEL — main-branch single writer (SDD §3.2, R-9):
#   * Evaluation entries are appended ONLY on the linear main history (post-merge), never by a
#     PR-time run. No two PRs ever touch this file concurrently -> no merge conflicts by construction.
#   * Adjudication (unadjudicated -> true-catch|false-positive) is an OPERATOR GIT COMMIT: the
#     operator edits the entry's `outcome` and commits it. Provenance = git authorship. A sensor
#     can NEVER self-adjudicate — `adjudicated_by` is a real git author, never the sensor.
#   * Tamper-evidence = the branch-protected main commit history (reflog/PR trail). No separate
#     signing layer; the git history IS the audit.
#
# EVALUATION RECORD SHAPE (one sensor run outcome):
#   {"ts":"<ISO-8601 UTC>","sensor":"<sensor-name>","seeded":<bool>,
#    "outcome":"true-catch|false-positive|clean|unadjudicated",
#    "adjudicated_by":"<git author or null>","pr":<number-or-null>}
#     - seeded:true            -> a deliberate break-then-revert fixture the sensor MUST catch (the
#                                 seeded qualifier, FR-4c). Only a seeded:true + true-catch can flip.
#     - outcome:clean          -> the sensor ran and found nothing (auto-resolved, no adjudication).
#     - outcome:unadjudicated  -> a flag awaiting the operator's verdict; BLOCKS promotion.
#     - outcome:true-catch     -> operator confirmed the flag was a real problem.
#     - outcome:false-positive -> operator confirmed the flag was wrong; the sensor cried wolf.
#
# PROMOTION EVENT SHAPE (written by tools/flip-promote.sh on an operator promote/rollback):
#   {"ts":"<ISO-8601 UTC>","sensor":"<sensor-name>","event":"promote|remove",
#    "blocking":<bool>,"adjudicated_by":"<git author>","pr":null}
#
# flip-report.sh reads the LAST N=10 evaluation entries per sensor for the rolling-window state
# (calibrating | flip-ready | blocking); older entries stay here forever as provenance.
#
# --- example (commented; the live ledger starts empty -> every sensor is `calibrating` at K=0/10) ---
# {"ts":"2026-07-03T00:00:00Z","sensor":"scope-checks","seeded":true,"outcome":"true-catch","adjudicated_by":"soju","pr":407}
# {"ts":"2026-07-03T00:01:00Z","sensor":"scope-checks","event":"promote","blocking":true,"adjudicated_by":"soju","pr":null}
